    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who secures our highest efficiency score of 81.21 against Bennett. The combination of an elite matchup against a 4.88 xERA arm and a prime #2 lineup spot creates a high-floor, high-ceiling scenario for home runs and RBI. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.07) follow closely; both benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Avila and Whisenhunt, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** in particular is a priority start as he faces an advantageous platoon split that boosts his value in our scarce SB categories, while **Drake Baldwin** continues to capitalize on strong recent form and a favorable pitching environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Brayan Rocchio**, who sits at 51.22\u2014just a hair shy of the utility threshold. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers decent versatility, he was edged out by the superior power-hitting context afforded to **Curtis Mead** (61.80) and **Gunnar Henderson** (64.32), despite the latter facing a tough assignment against Kirby. We are intentionally limiting **Sam Antonacci** (45.55) and **Nasim Nunez** (52.85) today; while their speed is vital to our roster construction, their #9 lineup positions drag their daily efficiency scores down, and they are essentially relegated to category-specific specialists today to avoid wasting plate appearances.\n\nManagers should monitor the risk surrounding **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, both of whom are running into a tough matchup against McClanahan. Their scores (59.54 and 57.55) hover right at the edge of our \"Strong\" start threshold. We remain cautious with **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to occupy a roster spot while on the IL, and we are hopeful that bench depth players like **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler** stay ready should the weather or late lineup shifts force a pivot. Today is all about efficiency; we are leaning into our high-leverage top-of-the-order hitters to drive production while keeping our bottom-order speed threats in restricted roles.",
